256
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:12,670
Huh?

257
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:14,460
What's that?

258
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:16,072
It's a virtual fortress.

259
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:20,852
Sensors indicate that all of the data
from Yu-Gi's duels is processed here.

260
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:24,237
You won't blow your
way through this thing.

261
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,849
It's the ultimate defense.

262
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:29,256
And it's impossible to
penetrate without the password.

263
00:16:30,460 --> 00:16:32,040
Hmm, a password.

264
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:34,240
If I know Pegasus,

265
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:36,757
that egomaniac would
never think that anyone

266
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:39,252
would outsmart him and get even this far.

267
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:40,900
We're going in.

268
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:42,330
The password?

269
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:44,700
Huh, Pegasus.

270
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,800
How can I defeat his
blue-eyes white dragon?

271
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:56,160
Yuki, you gotta admit for a
stiff, this Kaiba sure got game.

272
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:57,900
That's not my brother!

273
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,720
There's just no way!

274
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,340
Yuki, you know that's not him.

275
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,424
Everyone thinks he's a bad guy.

276
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:07,517
But I know my brother, and
he's not mean like this.

277
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:09,577
He's my best friend in the whole world.

278
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:11,360
That thing's not him.

279
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:14,580
You just gotta believe me.

280
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:17,037
I wish I could be as sure as you, Mokuba.

281
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:18,826
I don't know what to believe.

282
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:22,840
One thing I do know for sure,
this duel's not over yet.

283
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:27,320
Magical hats, conceal the dark magician.

284
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:33,040
He's under there somewhere, but which one?

285
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:38,528
Are you so desperate that you have your
dark magician doing simple hat tricks?

286
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:41,720
It's not a trick, and it's not so simple.

287
00:17:42,580 --> 00:17:45,817
Your move, but you better
think twice before you choose.

288
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:47,060
Just do the math.

289
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:51,580
Four hats, only 25 % chance
you'll find the Dark Magician.

290
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:56,140
The real question is, what else
is hiding beneath those hats?

291
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:57,700
Way to go, Yugi.

292
00:17:57,920 --> 00:18:01,097
Hey, now that's what I like to
call pulling one out of your hat.

293
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:02,640
Huh? All right!

294
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:05,980
You were right about the password.

295
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:08,241
The Virtual Fortress is unlocked.

296
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:11,940
We now have access to Yugi's
data, and it was just his turn.

297
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:15,217
Pegasus thinks he can make up
all the rules in this game,

298
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:18,297
but he could never have
imagined this brand new twist.

299
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:19,240
I'm back.

300
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:34,020
Hmm, so predictable.

301
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:36,237
I know where the Dark Magician hides.

302
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:38,820
If you're so sure, then move.

303
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:42,620
It's a shame this duel's
going to end so soon.

304
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:43,781
White Lightning!

305
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:51,900
If he attacks the right hat, I'll lose
more than just this duel. Much more!
